' Shishoza — UPDATED Sequence Diagram (adds submit-for-review + decision+email phases)
@startuml Shishoza_Sequence
actor "Citizen" as User
participant "Web App"        as W
participant "Flask API"      as A
participant "Geometry Engine" as G
database  "SQLite DB"        as D
participant "EE + RF Model"  as MOD
actor     "Forest Manager"   as FM
participant "Email / SMTP"   as SMTP

== Phase 1 — Parcel analysis ==
User -> W  : enter parcel
W -> A     : POST /api/analyse
A -> G     : resolve geometry
A -> MOD   : predict + 500m neighbourhood
A -> D     : cache analysis
A -> D     : log prediction (predictions_log.csv)
A --> W    : risk result

== Phase 2 — Cut simulation (opt) ==
User -> A  : POST /api/simulate
A --> W    : post-cut risk

== Phase 3 — Alternatives (alt: risk HIGH/MED) ==
User -> A  : POST /api/alternatives
A -> D     : lookup by reason
A --> W    : suggestions

== Phase 4 — Manager dashboard (auth) ==
FM -> A    : GET /manager
A -> D     : read cached sector aggregates
A --> FM   : district dashboard

== Phase 5 — Citizen submits parcel for review (NEW) ==
User -> A  : POST /api/requests
A -> D     : insert REQUESTS(status = pending)
A --> W    : submitted

== Phase 6 — Manager decision + citizen notified (NEW) ==
FM -> A    : POST /api/requests/{id}/decision
A -> D     : update REQUESTS(status, reviewed_by, note)
A -->> SMTP : async send decision email
SMTP -->> User : decision email
A --> FM   : ok

note over SMTP
  NEW vs report (was "6 lifelines, 4 phases"):
  +Forest Manager & +Email/SMTP lifelines,
  +Phase 5 (submit) & +Phase 6 (decision+async email)
  -> ~8 lifelines, 6 phases.
end note
@enduml
